IBus - Input Bus

Introduction
===

IBus is an Intelligent Input Bus. It is a new input framework for Linux OS
and an experimental port exists for macOS. It provides a full featured and
user friendly input method user interface. It also may help developers to
develop input methods easily.


How to build & test IBus
===

ibus-setup:
It is a gtk program to enable and configure ibus.

ibus:
It is ibus daemon.

hotkeys:
Super + Space: Change input method.

macOS:
An InputMethodKit client (`client/macos`) and Cocoa panel
(`ui/macospanel`) are built automatically on Darwin. See
`client/macos/README` for installing the IMK bundle.

For more detail please refer to https://github.com/ibus/ibus/wiki/ReadMe .


